From: piano-fedora <dev@piano.invalid>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] image: accept direct kernel entry into the launched UKI

systemd-stub 258 and newer, when Secure Boot is off or no shim is loaded,
enters the embedded kernel through the UKI's own entry point instead of
LoadImage()ing it as a child image. Before the jump it temporarily
rewrites the UKI's LoadedImage: ImageBase and ImageSize describe the
kernel, FilePath becomes a memory-mapped device path, and LoadOptions
carries the kernel cmdline. The fields are restored once the entry point
returns.

ExitBootServices is called from inside that entry point, so
ValidateInstalledEfiImage() observes the rewritten ImageBase/ImageSize
and rejects the UKI with EFI_ACCESS_DENIED. The kernel EFI stub turns
that into EFI_LOAD_ERROR, and the boot menu reports that the Linux image
format is unsupported.

Upstream does not see this: its rootfs is Debian trixie, whose systemd
257.13 always LoadImage()s the kernel in linux_exec(), so the parent
LoadedImage never changes and the comparison passes. A stub version of
258 or newer breaks it.

Gate the Base/Size comparison on the caller not being the UKI handle.
A directly entered kernel calls ExitBootServices with the UKI handle; a
LoadImage()ed kernel passes its own child handle. The UKI handle,
ParentHandle, DeviceHandle, image state and the parent-chain walk are
still checked, so only the two fields the stub documents as rewritten
are relaxed.
---
diff --git a/uefi/core/product/PianoProductCore.c b/uefi/core/product/PianoProductCore.c
index 569b32f..e142ff9 100644
--- a/uefi/core/product/PianoProductCore.c
+++ b/uefi/core/product/PianoProductCore.c
@@ -410,8 +410,12 @@ STATIC EFI_STATUS ValidateInstalledEfiImage(VOID *Context,EFI_HANDLE Image,CONST
   EFI_LOADED_IMAGE_PROTOCOL *Uki=NULL,*Current=NULL;
   EFI_STATUS Status=gBS->HandleProtocol(mLinuxApplication.Image,&gEfiLoadedImageProtocolGuid,(VOID **)&Uki);
   if(!BootLogAlive())return EFI_ABORTED;if(Status!=EFI_SUCCESS)return EfiImageResult("uki-protocol",Status);
+  // systemd-stub >= 258 without a shim enters the embedded kernel directly and
+  // temporarily rewrites this UKI's own LoadedImage to describe the kernel.
+  // The handle and its parents stay ours; only Base/Size move, so accept that
+  // for the image we started. Every other identity check stays strict.
   if(!EfiLoadedValid(Uki) || Uki!=mLinuxApplication.LoadedIdentity ||
-     Uki->ImageBase!=mLinuxApplication.BaseIdentity || Uki->ImageSize!=mLinuxApplication.SizeIdentity ||
+     (Image!=mLinuxApplication.Image && (Uki->ImageBase!=mLinuxApplication.BaseIdentity || Uki->ImageSize!=mLinuxApplication.SizeIdentity)) ||
      Uki->ParentHandle!=(EFI_HANDLE)Context || Uki->DeviceHandle!=mLinuxEsp)return EfiImageResult("uki-identity",EFI_ACCESS_DENIED);
   EFI_HANDLE Seen[4];EFI_HANDLE CurrentImage=Image;
   // The UKI loads its embedded kernel from memory. Only inner frames may lack
